    {
      "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@52964",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "BENVOLIO.\nAn if he hear thee, thou wilt anger him.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@52964/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@52964/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 50,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 5351964,
        "end": 5352044,
        "line": 198973,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap30/p@52964",
        "anchor": "sceneII_30.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "BENVOLIO.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MERCUTIO.\nThis cannot anger him. ’Twould anger him\nTo raise a spirit in his mistress’ circle,\nOf some strange nature, letting it there stand\nTill she had laid it, and conjur’d it down;\nThat were some spite. My invocation\nIs fair and honest, and, in his mistress’ name,\nI conjure only but to raise up him.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 50,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-3",
          "start": 51,
          "end": 93,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-4",
          "start": 94,
          "end": 140,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-5",
          "start": 141,
          "end": 184,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-6",
          "start": 185,
          "end": 220,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-7",
          "start": 221,
          "end": 268,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53048/line-8",
          "start": 269,
          "end": 304,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 5352048,
        "end": 5352412,
        "line": 198978,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap30/p@53048",
        "anchor": "sceneII_30.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "MERCUTIO.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53416",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "BENVOLIO.\nCome, he hath hid himself among these trees\nTo be consorted with the humorous night.\nBlind is his love, and best befits the dark.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53416/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53416/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 53,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53416/line-3",
          "start": 54,
          "end": 94,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53416/line-4",
          "start": 95,
          "end": 139,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 5352416,
        "end": 5352595,
        "line": 198989,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap30/p@53416",
        "anchor": "sceneII_30.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "BENVOLIO.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53599",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MERCUTIO.\nIf love be blind, love cannot hit the mark.\nNow will he sit under a medlar tree,\nAnd wish his mistress were that kind of fruit\nAs maids call medlars when they laugh alone.\nO Romeo, that she were, O that she were\nAn open-arse and thou a poperin pear!\nRomeo, good night. I’ll to my truckle-bed.\nThis field-bed is too cold for me to sleep.\nCome, shall we go?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53599/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53599/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 53,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53599/line-3",
          "start": 54,
          "end": 90,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53599/line-4",
          "start": 91,
          "end": 136,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53599/line-5",
          "start": 137,
          "end": 181,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "romeo-and-juliet/sceneII_30.1/p@53599/line-6",
          "start": 182,
          "end": 221,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
